Every printed part of the arm comes off a print plate, and each plate gets a timelapse here. Each timelapse is the X1C printer's own camera recording, sped up. An entry lists the part files on the plate, the material and settings, the layer count and the print time. It also links the milestones the parts belong to.

A plate still on the printer reads **Printing, timelapse coming** until its video is up.

The parts are [PETG](/lore/m2-one-joint); the official [Printing](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/build/printing/) page explains why. The [milestone videos](/lore/videos) are separate: they explain each step to camera.

<Timelapses />

## Terms

- **print plate**: the set of parts printed together in one print job.
